[dvystrcil/homelab] Monthly test restore of restic backup for Claude memory  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 43s, lane=claude)
## Why
The Claude Code memory is stored in a restic repository, but there is no automated verification that the backup can be successfully restored. Without periodic test restores, a backup may appear healthy yet be unusable when needed (e.g., after hardware failure or accidental corruption). This follows the pattern identified in https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1184 where scheduled checks were green because nothing asked them to work.

## What we know
- The Claude Code memory restic repository is referenced in https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1909 (Off-site copy of the Claude Code memory restic repo) and https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1951 (Off-site encrypted copy of CNPG backups).
- A similar pattern exists in `vt350/cad/backup-models.sh --verify`, which backs up FreeCAD models with restic and then verifies by restoring and comparing checksums.
- Homelab already has scheduled jobs for other backups (e.g., `etcd-backup`, `immich-db-backup`, `pihole-backup`, `vaultwarden-backup`) that run as CronJobs and complete successfully.
- The homelab uses restic for backups and has existing scripts in `bin/` (e.g., `bin/homelab-memory.sh`) that interact with the memory store.

**unverified**: Exact path to the restic repository and password file location for Claude memory backup; exact command to perform a non-destructive restore-and-verify test.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** A monthly CronJob runs a test restore of the Claude memory restic backup (no overwrite of live data), logs success/failure, and alerts on failure.
- [ ] **AC2.** The test restore command is derived from `bin/homelab-memory.sh` and restic best practices (restore to a temporary directory and verify integrity).
- [ ] **AC3.** The job is scheduled in a homelab CronJob manifest (e.g., under `homelab/cluster/` or `homelab/.github/workflows/`) and runs on the first day of each month.

## Lane
claude — requires design decisions: where to store the test restore (temp dir vs PVC), how to handle credentials securely, integration with existing alerting (e.g., Prometheus alerts via webhook), and coordination with off-site backup strategy (https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1909, https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1951).

